#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064009 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/id #uuid "4d4edfc8-e178-58b4-b827-e4310ead130e" :question/math-academy-id "e-485" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}-1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1} = 4 -\\dfrac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{4x-1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4x{|}_{0}^{1}-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[4-0]-5[\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1] \\\\  & =4-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064010 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/id #uuid "74761123-d539-5d78-8dcd-4ea1db04bed0" :question/math-academy-id "e-486" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division. \n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{ 2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3} .\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+3x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064011 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "cf016fa7-c3a2-5f9b-84a6-7b005d0d7286" :question/math-academy-id "e-487" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\textrm d x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x-1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}\\dfrac12$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $\\dfrac12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-\\dfrac12$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} & =1-\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329188 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc457955-dab3-5ba4-8f77-192fa422c9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329190} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9339b1-122b-59d1-8567-006b41ab76e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329191} {:answer/id #uuid "888ad65f-a721-54b1-b41c-34e3bc0c23f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}(1+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329192} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4ec236-5e1b-5724-97ef-8409b74f976c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329193} {:answer/id #uuid "e54e893f-8cf1-5283-9bd0-cea00ff72973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e54e893f-8cf1-5283-9bd0-cea00ff72973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329194} :answer-field/id #uuid "edbb6eef-4442-5b15-8560-cfa9b2fce45e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9cb05493-3a43-5cd7-9456-a6491428f397" :question/math-academy-id "q-114896" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $6$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & 2 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & 2 & \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} & =2+\\frac{(\\frac{2}{3})}{(x+\\frac{1}{6})} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{4}{6x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{2x+1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}(2+\\frac{4}{6x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{-1/12}^{0}\\frac{1}{6x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{4}{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[2x+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6x+1|]}_{-1/12}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(0-(-\\frac{1}{12}))+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(0)+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|6(-\\frac{1}{12})+1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[2(\\frac{1}{12})+\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}(1+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d79c989b-6593-5652-8d35-7984dcc4d651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329197} {:answer/id #uuid "48af1386-88ba-5186-b23c-fc6da9ac5045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d79c989b-6593-5652-8d35-7984dcc4d651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329197} :answer-field/id #uuid "54f57a12-9bed-5b83-bc99-22e551a8f2dd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9a6fd3e-be42-5fa6-b11c-40399135f34f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9a6fd3e-be42-5fa6-b11c-40399135f34f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329200} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2254b8e-e025-5f34-bb1b-88840799d44e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329199}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29ec841b-5e16-5ecb-8bc2-624dbc400c03" :question/math-academy-id "q-352219" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,23\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $8$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-24$ |\n|  | $8$ | $-23$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}=8-\\frac{23}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}(8-\\frac{23}{x+3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\text{d}x-23{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8x\\,{|}_{2}^{4}-23\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =8(4-2)-23(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+3|) \\\\  & =16-23(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) \\\\  & =16-23\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{7}{5}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a8d662c-a28d-5dfd-9f84-bd201ce8da28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a8d662c-a28d-5dfd-9f84-bd201ce8da28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329203} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c49b648-fb1f-5e74-9030-5004cd410fe7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329202} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb8bc45e-9e88-508e-9118-f6d3b447c114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb8bc45e-9e88-508e-9118-f6d3b447c114" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329205} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c6b66ef-9248-517c-bd70-4a8da2f2b42d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329204}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f3bfb7fe-e8c7-55e0-8fa0-25b966f35697" :question/math-academy-id "q-352220" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $9$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-36$ |\n|  | $9$ | $-29$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}=9-\\frac{29}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}(9-\\frac{29}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\text{d}x-29{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9x\\,{|}_{-1}^{2}-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =9(2-(-1))-29(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-1+4|) \\\\  & =27-29(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =27-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{3}) \\\\  & =27-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,2\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba322277-f833-5b0f-b6ff-1b153f0ed981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329208} {:answer/id #uuid "7b08c6d1-b0ef-5251-8fcd-8130d4bd8ff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b08c6d1-b0ef-5251-8fcd-8130d4bd8ff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329209} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8f13992-7cd8-53d4-bc5f-ebe64335c164" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68d838cc-4447-5437-91aa-e0933b13b858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68d838cc-4447-5437-91aa-e0933b13b858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329211} :answer-field/id #uuid "08551bad-3dfc-5628-ac2b-6fb8af17a13a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "72030db9-28d9-5270-aae9-585679ac8d61" :question/math-academy-id "q-352246" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $1$ | $8$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-4$ | $-16$ |\n|  | $1$ | $4$ | $-9$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}=x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x-9{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{3}+4x\\,{|}_{0}^{3}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{2}-{0}^{2})+4(3-0)-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+4|) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}+12-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{2}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{7}{4}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bacdac22-7c6b-5b85-b2f1-d72f1101efe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bacdac22-7c6b-5b85-b2f1-d72f1101efe9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329214} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4889729-35b6-598a-81ae-72b11a53eaa5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "be9ad5b5-e9ad-553d-b5f1-2e80ee4b4ad4" :question/math-academy-id "q-352247" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-7$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}=3{x}^{2}-4x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{3}-{1}^{3}]-2[{2}^{2}-{1}^{2}]+[2-1] \\\\  & =7\\cdot 1-2(3)+1 \\\\  & =7-6+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c25042b5-238c-561d-a835-d11002ded149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c25042b5-238c-561d-a835-d11002ded149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329217} :answer-field/id #uuid "744ab197-f2d4-5274-8f96-087886feaa13" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329216} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4ec6380-bbae-5d10-ab99-fe55633b30a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4ec6380-bbae-5d10-ab99-fe55633b30a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329219} :answer-field/id #uuid "2085e0d5-c4db-58ea-a66f-f821d9ef6442" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "22bd6b2f-502e-5ce3-99ef-deb51dae08a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-358835" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{11}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $2$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2(x+1/2)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{(x+1/2)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $5$ | $-3$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n|  | $5$ | $-\\frac{11}{2}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-3}{(x+1/2)} & =5-\\frac{(11/2)}{(x+1/2)} \\\\  & =5-\\frac{11}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{5x-3}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(5-\\frac{11}{2x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x-11{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[5x-\\frac{11}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5(1-0)-\\frac{11}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[5-\\frac{11\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{11}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329220 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e011deb-b0b4-5fd4-8afe-862e648f4515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329222} {:answer/id #uuid "f24a8ed1-7d98-5485-a8ea-4103a4484b38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e011deb-b0b4-5fd4-8afe-862e648f4515" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329222} :answer-field/id #uuid "95589281-5b67-5528-afdb-baf9b389e061" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329221} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69df8fcc-df88-5ffc-a68d-6b44fd7cf15b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69df8fcc-df88-5ffc-a68d-6b44fd7cf15b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329225} :answer-field/id #uuid "300819cd-134b-5280-af9f-cd770314968c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b6597e0e-678e-53cf-896b-1b7f4502efe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-358987" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\frac{7}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $3$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3(x-2/3)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{(x-2/3)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $4$ | $-5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $\\frac{8}{3}$ |\n|  | $4$ | $-\\frac{7}{3}$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-5}{(x-2/3)} & =4-\\frac{(7/3)}{(x-2/3)} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{7}{3x-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4x-5}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(4-\\frac{7}{3x-2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\text{d}x-7{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{3x-2}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[4x-\\frac{7}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3x-2|]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[4(3-1)-\\frac{7}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|7|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1|)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[8-\\frac{7\\operatorname{ln}⁡7}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-\\frac{7}{9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(7).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314904 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6aec6078-01a4-5b59-93d5-68b741df2d28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314906} {:answer/id #uuid "49eaa986-5e8a-5ee8-bfcb-04d71b74d6fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314907} {:answer/id #uuid "43207d35-a11f-5227-b363-5116699634ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314908} {:answer/id #uuid "6e7bc3a5-251e-5de7-9737-1b55ced5e7a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314909} {:answer/id #uuid "3e35a6e5-48f5-5ec7-92a6-fa0e877d97c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+7\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43207d35-a11f-5227-b363-5116699634ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314908} :answer-field/id #uuid "585def09-c78b-5de6-9b00-3dbc3c05e2dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8994c3eb-f396-5b4f-a637-dc6bb7953e49" :question/math-academy-id "q-49354" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7 \\\\  & ↓ & -10 \\\\  & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{5x+7}{x+2}=5-\\frac{3}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5x+7}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (5-\\frac{3}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\text{d}x-3\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac7904f-19ce-541b-9ac3-bd28f600e25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{3}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329228} {:answer/id #uuid "a991d633-29cf-517b-b6a6-d56774d2ab3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329229} {:answer/id #uuid "ea9e3dbe-b937-58b8-9363-fd41269fe2cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329230} {:answer/id #uuid "972880a6-8ea1-5a69-9541-a50a262281d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329231} {:answer/id #uuid "738bfa19-a25e-5250-94a7-2d2484b36938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ac7904f-19ce-541b-9ac3-bd28f600e25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{3}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329228} :answer-field/id #uuid "d86b8f94-f6d0-53df-a9e6-f2d867878db1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9156045e-7fa2-5298-b62c-0937c4d32fb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49357" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x+1}{4(x+\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4} & 1 & 1 \\\\  & ↓ & -\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & 1 & \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+1}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})} & =1+\\frac{(\\frac{3}{4})}{(x+\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{3}{4(x+\\frac{1}{4})} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{3}{4x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int (1+\\frac{3}{4x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\int \\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{4x+1}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[x+\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{3}{16}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61f4887b-3d01-58b1-bcd9-d2fb19997842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314913} {:answer/id #uuid "2e147fd6-0f93-5c00-8018-d07ef10f0ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314914} {:answer/id #uuid "2708a6b9-fb75-5c92-9425-f57e1167c066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314915} {:answer/id #uuid "8f75d583-8a2e-5cf8-a698-0af2fdc387f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314916} {:answer/id #uuid "c248c35d-9a92-551e-802d-626ecaaa5da8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2708a6b9-fb75-5c92-9425-f57e1167c066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314915} :answer-field/id #uuid "461040fd-6236-57ff-af4a-4babd622bde1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fef7e5a4-8743-520c-8404-5503ee85f90a" :question/math-academy-id "q-49398" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+4}{x+3}=1+\\frac{1}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{x+4}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}(1+\\frac{1}{x+3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-2}^{0}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{|}_{-2}^{0}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|{|}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =(0-(-2))+(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-2+3|) \\\\  & =2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236f51c2-22ad-551f-afb4-62fd6de6d21e" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Quotient of Linear Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc50da8-06cb-577e-8f11-1aff146f7f81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329235} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d532aa-8958-5aa1-b8cf-7fbdf8c1e823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329236} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c8c753-e20b-5a57-9747-dedcf8624012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329237} {:answer/id #uuid "fe03f578-571b-540d-9ef3-181a8e51e77c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329238} {:answer/id #uuid "95478d83-2b74-54d6-b2ce-4b4d621257a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dc50da8-06cb-577e-8f11-1aff146f7f81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329235} :answer-field/id #uuid "949bdaac-b6c0-5c99-bf9e-a00284063bb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b29eab9-2700-5c7a-9162-4cf65ec05697" :question/math-academy-id "q-49411" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3x-2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\  & ↓ & -3 \\\\  & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x-2}{x+1}=3-\\frac{5}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x-2}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3-\\frac{5}{x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3x-5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b57d584-29e0-514d-8ce7-8bf95af333ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314934} {:answer/id #uuid "0dcd9336-343a-59a5-ae33-3e75a9e8f1de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314935} {:answer/id #uuid "953549fb-6843-5e38-a909-0b2d32bb2e7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314936} {:answer/id #uuid "66c47afb-0399-5e9b-bb15-85438050f36b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314937} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0308f5-8d24-5bea-8cea-4b6d5f17f3ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b57d584-29e0-514d-8ce7-8bf95af333ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314934} :answer-field/id #uuid "06777435-7464-543f-9a23-0ac5af9f8489" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1b477fe5-67ac-5170-be29-6f6d97baa23e" :question/math-academy-id "q-49456" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 3 & 3 & -9 & 1 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 9 & 0 & 3 \\\\  & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}=3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+x-1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}+1+\\frac{2}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}+x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b43ee77e-72d0-5d5f-b330-cd6323b7c326" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329242} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab2c672-ea2f-591b-a6e6-5db800760e44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329243} {:answer/id #uuid "d6efbcbb-0082-5883-b3ca-24de6877d7c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329244} {:answer/id #uuid "28fcf979-ed78-5f4c-873a-9d463851fb72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329245} {:answer/id #uuid "7343b116-ffdf-5ff8-bfd1-c0af3a62c4fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6efbcbb-0082-5883-b3ca-24de6877d7c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329244} :answer-field/id #uuid "90febbfa-f053-5bdc-8df9-47ca6db870a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1fe983d-a812-574b-a770-af40f5ba5920" :question/math-academy-id "q-49457" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+10}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -5 & 1 & 7 & 10 \\\\  & ↓ & -5 & -10 \\\\  & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+10}{x+5}=x+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+7x+10}{x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+2)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1}+2x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}]+2[1-0] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f110daa3-fd31-5e34-8a88-0e002c2e418a" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator is Linear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98ab4987-2a41-5a6d-83a7-c8c16687755d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{2}x-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329249} {:answer/id #uuid "1ba17ce9-7b82-5167-9964-a423e881e326" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329250} {:answer/id #uuid "c52c9408-bf3d-53ad-bc0c-046483dd7202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-6x-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-2|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329251} {:answer/id #uuid "e778c959-be05-5546-be89-1b654eef9bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329252} {:answer/id #uuid "25fa8cc0-437f-50fe-927a-666aef4fbdcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e778c959-be05-5546-be89-1b654eef9bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329252} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9f45fc8-1d4f-501e-bd8a-601eea9dbece" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329248}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "910ac292-9317-5cd0-9e18-28f3dc011864" :question/math-academy-id "q-49460" :question/problem "$\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-6}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ 2 & 1 & -2 & 3 & -6 \\\\  & ↓ & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\  & 1 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-6}{x-2}={x}^{2}+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3x-6}{x-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int ({x}^{2}+3)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+3x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7d71bc2-c0f0-5504-9f79-a5f5cdb8cd92" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Rational Function Whose Denominator Contains a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b60b452-aacd-56fd-b7af-9b124c7c01d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329256} {:answer/id #uuid "fd4d0715-faea-5b22-87f5-e07729136917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329257} {:answer/id #uuid "26c59c69-aef0-5756-a801-b22197849d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329258} {:answer/id #uuid "dd051e7f-653f-553d-8e8a-9cae7e72c20e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329259} {:answer/id #uuid "986b5070-d35a-5a1f-b8fb-7d0830d61f54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd4d0715-faea-5b22-87f5-e07729136917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329257} :answer-field/id #uuid "11558995-4bba-5309-bf1c-92b647e9d322" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33ca9b7c-fc9e-559a-a429-545cdd28eedd" :question/math-academy-id "q-73390" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we pull out the factor of $4$ from the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4(x-\\frac{3}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{8x-1}{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we draw up our synthetic division table to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & x & {x}^{0} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & 8 & -1 \\\\  & ↓ & 6 \\\\  & 8 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x-1}{(x-\\frac{3}{4})} & =8+\\frac{5}{(x-\\frac{3}{4})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{8x-1}{4x-3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int (8+\\frac{5}{x-\\frac{3}{4}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8\\int \\text{d}x+5\\int \\frac{1}{x-\\frac{3}{4}}\\,\\text{d}x] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[8x+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|]+C \\\\  & =2x+\\frac{5}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-\\frac{3}{4}|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
